From 4e5ab326b6bff4910b64f4f42f9b8ffd7a855c16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:04:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kasir): actually right-align the toolbar icons (previous
 commit was broken)

The previous commit left Filter/Grid pinned to the left edge with the
search bar stretched out next to them, because the search bar was
wrapped in Expanded unconditionally -- with no Spacer before Filter/Grid,
there was nothing pushing the cluster to the right. Screenshot from the
device confirmed this: icons crammed left, big blank white search pill
taking the rest of the row.

Fix:
- Add a Spacer() before Filter/Grid/Search when NOT searching, so the
  three idle icons form a tight right-aligned cluster (verified against
  a Playwright screenshot of the approved HTML reference, which used
  the same flex-filler approach and was correct all along)
- Search control extracted into _SearchBarSurface: idle renders as a
  plain 44x44 circle (identical size/shadow to Filter/Grid, holding only
  the search glyph, no visible TextField); searching wraps it in
  Expanded so it grows from the left edge once Filter/Grid/Spacer have
  collapsed away. Previously the search 'circle' was actually always a
  full Expanded pill with an invisible-but-present TextField squeezed
  next to the icon, which is why it rendered oddly at idle.
- Removed now-dead _animDuration/_animCurve fields on _KasirToolbar.
